# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# TheDraw font bundles and their .TDX index sidecars are binary. `* text=auto`
# above would otherwise be trusted to auto-detect them; state it explicitly so
# line-ending normalization can never silently corrupt a 21 MB glyph bundle.
*.TDF binary
*.TDX binary

# Override GitHub language detection so QB64-PE sources get syntax highlighting.
# Verified with real github-linguist (crazymax/linguist): all of .BAS/.BI/.BM
# resolve 100% to QuickBASIC, whose grammar is derived from QB64's own VS Code
# grammar -- the best-fitting highlight for QB64-PE code.
#
# Two things this MUST get right, both of which the previous version got wrong:
#   1. LANGUAGE NAME: the value must be a language Linguist actually ships a
#      grammar for. "qb64" is NOT one -> the override was ignored, Linguist fell
#      back to raw extension guessing, and most files went unclassified. The
#      correct token is "QuickBASIC". (FreeBASIC / BASIC also work but use
#      VB.NET / generic-BASIC grammars, a worse fit -- swap + re-push to compare.)
#   2. CASE: .gitattributes patterns are case-sensitive. DRAW's files are
#      UPPERCASE (.BAS/.BI/.BM/.FRM), so lowercase `*.bas` patterns never matched.
#      Both cases are listed below so it works regardless.
#
# NOTE: a linguist-language override only takes effect once this file is
# COMMITTED and the repo is viewed on github.com -- you cannot confirm it locally.
*.BAS linguist-language=QuickBASIC
*.BI  linguist-language=QuickBASIC
*.BM  linguist-language=QuickBASIC
*.FRM linguist-language=QuickBASIC
*.bas linguist-language=QuickBASIC
*.bi  linguist-language=QuickBASIC
*.bm  linguist-language=QuickBASIC
*.frm linguist-language=QuickBASIC
# ANSI-art files are byte-exact (CRLF, CP437 high bytes, binary headers) — never normalize
*.ans   -text
*.asc   -text
*.nfo   -text
*.diz   -text
*.bin   -text
*.xb    -text
*.xbin  -text
*.tnd   -text
